{"name":"Pochard Duck Head","hex":"#ee9977","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pochard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various diving ducks of the subfamily Aythyinae (genera Aythya and Netta), especially the common pochard, Aythya ferina."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pochard"},{"term":"duck","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To quickly lower (the head or body), often in order to prevent it from being struck by something.","To lower (something) into water; to thrust or plunge under liquid and suddenly withdraw."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cave passage containing water with low, or no, airspace."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duck"},{"term":"head","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of the body of an animal or human which contains the brain, mouth, and main sense organs.","To do with heads.\nMental or emotional aptitude or skill."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or intended for the head."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/head"}],"entries":[{"title":"Duck Head","blocks":[{"text":"Duck Head is a brand name for clothing and shoes in the United States. First registered as a trademark in the late 19th century, the name has been used by several different manufacturers and retailers of apparel, primarily in the American South. Duck Head apparel had a period of great popularity in the 1980s and early 1990s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/80/Duckhead2.JPG/330px-Duckhead2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duck_Head","wikidata":"Q16992088"},{"title":"Pochard","blocks":[{"text":"Pochard is a common name used for several species of diving ducks:"},{"items":["Four species in the genus Aythya:\nCommon pochard, Aythya ferina\nBaer's pochard, Aythya baeri\nFerruginous pochard, Aythya nyroca\nMadagascar pochard, Aythya innotata","Common pochard, Aythya ferina","Baer's pochard, Aythya baeri","Ferruginous pochard, Aythya nyroca","Madagascar pochard, Aythya innotata","Three species in the genus Netta:\nRed-crested pochard, Netta rufina\nRosy-billed pochard or Rosybill, Netta peposaca\nSouthern pochard, Netta erythrophthalma","Red-crested pochard, Netta rufina","Rosy-billed pochard or Rosybill, Netta peposaca","Southern pochard, Netta erythrophthalma"]},{"items":["Common pochard, Aythya ferina","Baer's pochard, Aythya baeri","Ferruginous pochard, Aythya nyroca","Madagascar pochard, Aythya innotata"]},{"items":["Red-crested pochard, Netta rufina","Rosy-billed pochard or Rosybill, Netta peposaca","Southern pochard, Netta erythrophthalma"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pochard","wikidata":"Q7206321"},{"title":"Duck","blocks":[{"text":"Duck is the common name for numerous species of waterfowl in the family Anatidae. Ducks are generally smaller and shorter-necked than swans and geese, which are members of the same family. Divided among several subfamilies, they are a form taxon; they do not represent a monophyletic group, since swans and geese are not considered ducks. Ducks are mostly aquatic birds, and may be found in both fresh water and sea water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Bucephala-albeola-010.jpg/330px-Bucephala-albeola-010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duck","wikidata":"Q3736439"},{"title":"Head","blocks":[{"text":"A head is the part of an organism which usually includes the ears, brain, forehead, cheeks, chin, eyes, nose, and mouth, each of which aids in various sensory functions such as sight, hearing, smell, and taste. Some very simple animals may not have a head, but many bilaterally symmetric forms do, regardless of size."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Portrait_of_a_Meerkat.jpg/330px-Portrait_of_a_Meerkat.jpg